# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, how line endings get stored depends on each machine's
# core.autocrlf setting rather than on the repository. Yours is set correctly
# today, so everything in here is already stored with Unix line endings, but
# that is luck rather than a rule. This makes it a rule, so a second machine,
# a fresh clone, or Vercel's Linux builder all agree.
#
# "text=auto" means: decide per file whether it is text, and if it is, store it
# with LF. Your working copy on Windows still gets CRLF, so nothing about how
# you edit changes.
* text=auto

# Recipe files are the content of the site, so be explicit about them.
*.txt text
*.md text

# Code and config.
*.ts text
*.tsx text
*.js text
*.mjs text
*.cjs text
*.astro text
*.css text
*.json text
*.svg text
*.html text

# Binary files git must never try to convert. Doing so corrupts them.
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary

# package-lock.json is generated. Marking it means a merge conflict in it shows
# as one blob to regenerate rather than thousands of lines to read by hand.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
